### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- description: Detect new Bear notes tagged #share, extract content into JSON Canvas knowledge nodes, update agent_capabilities.canvas, and broadcast previews via BlueBubbles. Use when syncing Bear notes to canvas and group chat, or when asked to "sync shared notes", "distribute Bear notes", or "publish #share notes".
- Sync Bear notes tagged `#share` → JSON Canvas nodes → BlueBubbles group chat.
- - Bear running with grizzly CLI installed (`go install github.com/tylerwince/grizzly/cmd/grizzly@latest`)
- - Bear API token at `~/.config/grizzly/token`
- - BlueBubbles channel configured in gateway (`channels.bluebubbles`)
- - State file at `~/.openclaw/skills/bear-share-sync/state.json` tracks processed note IDs
- ### 1. Poll for new #share notes
- grizzly open-tag --name "share" --enable-callback --json --token-file ~/.config/grizzly/token
- Parse the JSON response to get note list. Compare against `state.json` to find unprocessed notes.
- ### 2. Extract note content
- For each new note, read full content:
- grizzly open-note --id "NOTE_ID" --enable-callback --json
- Extract: title, body (strip `#share` tag), creation date.
- ### 3. Update agent_capabilities.canvas
- Read the existing canvas file, append a new text node with:
- - `id`: `bear-<note-id>` (sanitized)
- - `type`: `text`
- - `text`: formatted summary (title + first 200 chars + source link)
- - `x`: auto-positioned (max existing x + 300, or 0 if empty)
- - `y`: auto-positioned (next row at y+200 when column exceeds 4 nodes)
- - `width`: 260, `height`: 120
- - `color`: `"4"` (green)
- Add an edge from the new node to a central "Shared Notes" group node if one exists.
- Write the updated canvas JSON back.
- ### 4. Send preview via BlueBubbles
- ```json
- {
- {
-   "action": "send",
-   "channel": "bluebubbles",
-   "target": "<GROUP_CHAT_GUID>",
-   "message": "📝 New shared note: <TITLE>\n\n<PREVIEW_TEXT>\n\n— via Bear #share"
- }
- }
- ### 5. Update state
- Append processed note ID and timestamp to `state.json`.
- See [references/config.md](references/config.md) for configurable parameters (group chat GUID, canvas path, preview length).
- ## State File
- `state.json` format:
-   "processed": [
-     { "id": "NOTE_ID", "title": "Note Title", "processedAt": "2026-05-12T03:00:00Z" }
-   ]
- ## Automation
- Set up a cron job to run this sync periodically:
- openclaw cron add --schedule "every 15m" --payload '{"kind":"agentTurn","message":"Run bear-share-sync: poll #share notes, update canvas, send previews"}'
- ## Scripts
- - [scripts/sync.sh](scripts/sync.sh) — End-to-end sync script (poll → extract → canvas → notify → state update)
